00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:42.720 line:100%
WEIYANG PUBLIC
SECURITY BUREAU NANSHAN BRANCH

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.960 line:20%
ARCHIVE REGISTRY

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:49.480 line:100%
Here it is. Yuanlongli, June 30th case,

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.640 line:100%
C2643.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.760 line:100%
ARCHIVES ROOM

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.120 line:100%
Mr. Xia, you've only been here a few days.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.800 line:100%
How are you so familiar with this place?

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.040 line:100%
Only a few days?

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.040 line:100%
I was already working here
before you even got here.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.400 line:100%
Later, when you were
assigned here after graduation,

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.400 line:100%
I was transferred to the logistics office.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.320 line:100%
What a coincidence.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.760 line:100%
Before my dad retired,
he was in logistics too.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.200 line:100%
I took over his post.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.040 line:100%
I've been filling in for your family.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:32.480 line:100%
Thank you so much.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:36.400 line:100%
If Captain Ran hadn't kept pushing
the higher-ups

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:39.280 line:100%
for funding and gotten
this archive room built,

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.920 line:100%
finding all these old files

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.200 line:100%
wouldn't have been easy.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.720 line:100%
That's right.
All the equipment here is the best.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.560 line:100%
Even the system
was built with upgrade ports.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.080 line:100%
It won't be outdated in a decade.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.520 line:100%
Back when Captain Ran was still here,

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.040 line:100%
he loved spending time
in this archive room.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.560 line:100%
Sometimes when I looked up,

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:01.280 line:100%
I'd almost think
he was still sitting right there,

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.760 line:100%
turning through files page by page.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.640 line:100%
These are all the files
from the June 30th case.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:33.960 line:100%
I won't keep disturbing you.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.080 line:100%
Want something to drink?

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.680 line:100%
Plain water is fine. Thank you, Mr. Xia.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.520 line:100%
Alright. Go ahead with it.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.520 line:100%
LIST OF EVIDENCE

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.480 line:100%
Pattia's staff badge.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.600 line:100%
MENGMENG NO.23

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:49.800 line:100%
Black robe.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.280 line:100%
Cigarette butt.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:54.960 line:100%
Letter.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.080 line:100%
Herbal medicine bag.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.280 line:100%
Wrench.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.200 line:100%
Photo of the trunk.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.080 line:100%
Blue leather heels.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.440 line:100%
Where are they?

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.480 line:100%
Xiaohe, what's wrong?

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.600 line:100%
Mr. Xia, if something was added later
to the evidence box,

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.040 line:100%
could it have been missed in the records?

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.920 line:100%
Absolutely impossible.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.280 line:100%
Whether evidence is stored
or someone checks it out,

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.240 line:100%
it must be recorded.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.360 line:100%
Checked out?

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.000 line:100%
PHYSICAL EVIDENCE CHECKOUT LOGBOOK

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:36.480 line:100%
GLOVES

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.240 line:100%
PHYSICAL EVIDENCE CHECKOUT FORM

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.760 line:100%
YUANLONGLI JUNE 30TH
A PAIR OF BLUE LEATHER HEELS

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.760 line:100%
CHECKED OUT BY: RAN FANGXU
STATUS: NOT RETURNED

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:50.800 line:100%
CHECKED OUT BY: RAN FANGXU
STATUS: NOT RETURNED

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.200 line:100%
Xiaohe?

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:54.840 line:100%
Ms. Liang Juan.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.320 line:100%
Isn't the task force on break?
Why are you here?

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.200 line:100%
I came to look
into the June 30th case files.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:02.680 line:100%
The June 30th case?

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.600 line:100%
Wasn't that closed
more than ten years ago?

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:05.560 line:100%
What's left to investigate?

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:06.560 line:100%
I want to look

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.440 line:100%
into a pair of blue leather heels
from the case.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.760 line:100%
Ms. Liang, do you know about that?

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.080 line:100%
Blue leather heels?

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:17.480 line:100%
Blue leather heels…

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:19.960 line:100%
Captain Ran asked about them before.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.280 line:100%
Captain Ran.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.320 line:100%
Captain Ran.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.200 line:100%
What new theory are you working on now?

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.560 line:100%
I'm thinking about everyday things,
like food and clothing.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.280 line:100%
Right, perfect timing.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:56.760 line:100%
In your view, a pair of red leather heels

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:58.000 line:100%
or a pair of blue leather heels,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.440 line:100%
which goes better with clothes?

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.640 line:100%
That depends on what shade
of red and blue.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:03.840 line:100%
Mm.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.560 line:100%
This cucumber is good.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.720 line:100%
The red and this blue.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:19.080 line:100%
Which would you choose?

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.640 line:100%
The red one is better.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:23.600 line:100%
Right. Blue doesn't go well with pants.

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:26.960 line:100%
What if you wrapped blue leather

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.680 line:100%
over red shoes?

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:30.800 line:100%
Would you wear that?

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:40.560 line:100%
Wrapped blue leather over red shoes?

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:43.640 line:100%
Look, he really had
terrible straight-man taste.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.760 line:100%
BLUE LEATHER HEELS

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:52.160 line:100%
Wait. I clearly remember Ran telling me

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:53.720 line:100%
those blue leather heels were lost.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.720 line:100%
<i>How were they checked out?</i>

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.720 line:100%
That signature is in
Uncle Ran's handwriting.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.320 line:100%
I couldn't mistake it.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.440 line:100%
<i>Maybe you weren't in good health</i>
<i>at that time.</i>

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.960 line:100%
<i>He didn't want you to worry more.</i>

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.880 line:100%
By the way, I ran
into Ms. Liang Juan just now.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.400 line:100%
She said in the winter of 2002,
Uncle Ran mentioned something about

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:10.200 line:100%
"wrapped blue leather over red shoes".

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.400 line:100%
Wrapped blue leather over red shoes?

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.440 line:100%
Maybe Uncle Ran thought

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.680 line:100%
those blue leather heels were fake.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.400 line:100%
Fake shoes?

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:20.520 line:100%
True.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:22.680 line:100%
There were plenty of counterfeit
leather shoes back in the 1990s.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.960 line:100%
The fakest kind
were those cardboard shoes.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.840 line:100%
<i>You know, hard cardboard</i>
<i>covered with artificial leather.</i>

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.320 line:100%
Then that explains it.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.960 line:100%
Once cardboard shoes get soaked,
the outer layer peels off.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.800 line:100%
Ran must've realized then

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.240 line:100%
that those blue leather heels were fake.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.400 line:100%
But how could fake shoes

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.280 line:100%
be an important clue?

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.160 line:100%
Thank you.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.200 line:100%
Welcome.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:25.240 line:100%
Serve him a drink.

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:27.280 line:100%
-No, thanks.
-Alright, sir.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.880 line:100%
Officer He, wasn't Mengmeng's case
solved ages ago?

00:08:31.959 --> 00:08:33.359 line:100%
Why are you investigating it again?

00:08:35.719 --> 00:08:37.880 line:100%
When Xu Meng was at Pattia,

00:08:37.959 --> 00:08:40.599 line:100%
did she wear
a pair of Double Fish high heels?

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:41.760 line:100%
Blue in color.

00:08:41.839 --> 00:08:43.640 line:100%
If I remember correctly,

00:08:43.719 --> 00:08:45.760 line:100%
the girls working at Pattia

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:47.920 line:100%
wore uniforms custom-made by the boss

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.480 line:100%
from head to toe.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:52.160 line:100%
But whether she wore them later
at the foot massage shop,

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.280 line:100%
I wouldn't know.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.680 line:100%
In 2002,

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:00.280 line:100%
did Officer Ran ask you anything else?

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:04.720 line:100%
I remember that rainy day in 1997.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.520 line:100%
FASHION BOUTIQUE

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:09.680 line:100%
Thank you. Su Yuzhi,

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:12.200 line:100%
wishing you booming business.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:18.400 line:100%
Bye.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.760 line:100%
That was the last time
I saw the handsome guy.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.440 line:100%
Mr. Ran is such a pity.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:34.240 line:100%
He was a nice guy.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.160 line:100%
He was gone just like that.

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:49.720 line:100%
Hello, Ms. Lili.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.000 line:100%
Officer He,

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.800 line:100%
it's been a long while.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.760 line:100%
I'm Lili. Don't you remember me?

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:08.520 line:100%
I wasn't close to Mengmeng.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:11.080 line:100%
I don't know anything
about what happened to her.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.400 line:100%
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION FILES

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:22.760 line:100%
BLUE LEATHER HEELS WORN BY XU MENG

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.360 line:100%
ON THE DAY SHE DISAPPEARED
WERE FOUND INSIDE WU SHANLONG'S HOME

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.640 line:100%
All arranged by color.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:45.880 line:100%
Wu Shanlong shows signs
of obsessive behavior.

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:05.120 line:100%
In 2002,

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:08.440 line:100%
Officer Ran came to see me.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.440 line:100%
I remember it was very cold that day.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:15.440 line:100%
-Here. Have some warm water.
-Thank you.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.760 line:100%
Here's our signature dish,
Spicy Stewed <i>Mao Xue Wang</i>.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:20.920 line:100%
Please enjoy your meal.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.440 line:100%
Officer Ran, you ordered so much food.

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.360 line:100%
There are only two of us.
We can't finish all this.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:27.600 line:100%
You shouldn't have spent so much.

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:30.080 line:100%
Not at all. If we can't
finish it, we can pack it up.

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:32.200 line:100%
Thank you, Officer Ran.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.720 line:100%
You're welcome. I still need your help.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:39.560 line:100%
Can you try to recall

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.000 line:100%
whether Xu Meng wore
a pair of blue leather heels

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:44.480 line:100%
when working at the foot massage shop?

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:46.400 line:100%
Blue leather heels?

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:51.240 line:100%
Yes. Yes, she did.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.960 line:100%
Those blue leather heels
were tall and eye-catching.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:57.120 line:100%
You know how it was

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:59.080 line:100%
working at the foot massage shop.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:01.280 line:100%
Everyone dressed flashy

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:03.480 line:100%
to attract customers and earn more money.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.720 line:100%
Were those shoes real
or fake cardboard shoes?

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:09.400 line:100%
Definitely real.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:11.800 line:100%
Mengmeng wasn't well-off,

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.160 line:100%
but she was very picky
about clothes and appearances.

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:16.000 line:100%
She would never wear fake shoes.

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:18.520 line:100%
Besides, we worked at a foot massage shop,

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:19.760 line:100%
so our shoes often got wet.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:22.760 line:100%
If they were cardboard shoes,
they would've fallen apart long ago.

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:27.000 line:100%
How could this be?

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:30.720 line:100%
That expression.

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:33.720 line:100%
Officer Ran had that same look
you have right now.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:42.200 line:100%
<i>The number you've dialed</i>
<i>is currently on another call.</i>

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.520 line:100%
<i>Please try again later.</i>

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:47.560 line:100%
<i>The number you've dialed</i>
<i>is currently on another call.</i>

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:48.960 line:100%
DAD

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.680 line:100%
<i>The number you've dialed</i>

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:53.160 line:100%
<i>is currently on another call.</i>

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.040 line:100%
KIDDO

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.440 line:100%
-<i>Hello?</i>
-Hello?

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:11.040 line:100%
-Who were you talking to?
-Who were you talking to?

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.080 line:100%
-I found something.
-I found something.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:14.800 line:100%
-Wu Shanlong was framed.
-Wu Shanlong was framed.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:46.680 line:100%
Are you alright?

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:53.520 line:100%
Dad, are you going to run away from home

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.440 line:100%
-and leave the case aside?
-Who said I'm leaving the case aside?

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:57.960 line:100%
I'm looking into it elsewhere.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:03.240 line:100%
Where are you going?

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.880 line:100%
What exactly is going on?

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:09.680 line:100%
Come.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:13.600 line:100%
Look at this.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.160 line:100%
You're observant.

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:19.240 line:100%
The shoes on this rack
are arranged by color.

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:21.640 line:100%
Only this pair of blue leather heels
is in the wrong place.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:24.960 line:100%
Whoever used fake blue leather heels
to frame Wu Shanlong

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:27.520 line:100%
must've known his daily routine
extremely well.

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:30.320 line:100%
They slipped in secretly while he was out.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:32.600 line:100%
But after all that planning,

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.920 line:100%
they overlooked one thing,
Wu Shanlong's obsessive habits.

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:38.480 line:100%
Also, I thought it through carefully.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:41.640 line:100%
The person who could frame Wu Shanlong

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:44.040 line:100%
would need to meet all four conditions.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:47.480 line:100%
First, they held a grudge
against Xu Meng and her father

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:48.800 line:100%
or were paid to kill them.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:52.120 line:100%
Second, they had to be able
to kill both of them

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.240 line:100%
and dismember the bodies.

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:55.040 line:100%
That would require
considerable physical strength…

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:55.960 line:100%
NAME LIST

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.080 line:100%
…and technical skills.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:01.520 line:100%
Third, before the police
found Wu Shanlong,

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.360 line:100%
they already knew he had a fetish

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:06.280 line:100%
and also knew what kinds of things
he liked collecting.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:11.000 line:100%
Fourth, they knew Yuanlongli
like the back of their hand

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.720 line:100%
and knew how to avoid the cameras.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:13.720 line:100%
At the same time,

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:16.520 line:100%
they could keep track
of Wu Shanlong's movements.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:20.760 line:100%
I went over everyone on the list.

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:22.520 line:100%
None of them fit.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:26.720 line:100%
Dad, you went in such a big circle
and ended up back at square one.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:28.880 line:100%
Doesn't that mean
you found nothing at all?

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.880 line:100%
How is that nothing?

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:33.560 line:100%
If we've gone back to square one,

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:35.440 line:100%
Ran would've gone back too.

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:38.680 line:100%
He must've hit a dead end
when he got here.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.320 line:100%
Think about it.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.480 line:100%
Where would he investigate next?

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:51.520 line:100%
<i>DE-PARADOXIFICATION IN CRIMINAL CASEWORK</i>

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:56.840 line:100%
The center is right here. Yuanlongli.

00:15:56.920 --> 00:16:00.040 line:100%
EVERY EVENT HAS A CENTER
BEYOND THE CENTER, THERE ARE RIPPLES

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:06.640 line:100%
Should've said that earlier.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:10.720 line:100%
NEW YORK BLOCK

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.040 line:100%
Mr. He. Mr. He.

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:21.200 line:100%
Mr. He, are you a chum salmon?

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:23.800 line:100%
What are you doing? Swimming upstream?

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.120 line:100%
What are you talking about?

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:27.560 line:100%
Isn't this building
a month away from demolition?

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:28.640 line:100%
You know it's being torn down,

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:30.360 line:100%
so why is a respected officer like you

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:31.720 line:100%
coming here to cause trouble?

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:33.360 line:100%
I promise I won't cause trouble.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:34.960 line:100%
I'm just here to relive
old times for a few days.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:37.280 line:100%
When demolition starts,
I won't hold anyone back.

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:38.240 line:100%
I'll move out on time.

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:42.360 line:100%
Mr. He. Mr. He.

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:44.040 line:100%
Mr. He…

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:51.040 line:100%
Almost there.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.080 line:100%
This is Wang Wuluan's unit.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.960 line:100%
In the whole building,
this is the only apartment left for rent.

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:06.520 line:100%
-Are you alright?
-I'm fine.

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:30.000 line:100%
You actually paid rent for this?

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:31.280 line:100%
There are many units here.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.720 line:100%
Couldn't you just pick one?

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:34.840 line:100%
You see, you're too green.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.640 line:100%
Stop. Leave that for now.

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:45.520 line:100%
Put the kettle on, make tea,
and wait for visitors.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:58.960 line:100%
This run-down place, jeez.

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:03.640 line:100%
Coming.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.160 line:100%
Officer He.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.240 line:100%
-Officer He.
-Come on in.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:12.480 line:100%
Officer He.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:15.400 line:100%
-Officer He, you moved in.
-It's messy.

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:17.000 line:100%
-Come in.
-Hello, Officer He.

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:19.280 line:100%
There's no need to hold back
in Officer He's place.

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:24.760 line:100%
Everyone, let's welcome Officer He
to his new home.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.440 line:100%
Welcome!

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:30.520 line:100%
Officer He. Officer He.
You came at the right time.

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:33.080 line:100%
It's great. We have a capable man
on our side now.

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.080 line:100%
Exactly. A capable helper.

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:38.480 line:100%
I came here with a mission.

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:42.080 line:100%
I need you and everyone
to help me ask around.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.760 line:100%
Everything about Officer Ran

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:47.080 line:100%
in Yuanlongli during the winter of 2002.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:49.960 line:100%
Who he met. What he did. What he said.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.840 line:100%
I want all of it.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:55.080 line:100%
Don't worry. You can count on us.

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.680 line:100%
-Right.
-No problem.

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:57.960 line:100%
Of course.

00:18:58.040 --> 00:19:00.800 line:100%
Looks like not everyone came today.

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:02.880 line:100%
I suggest we create a group chat.

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:03.800 line:100%
-Sure.
-Right.

00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:06.720 line:100%
If anyone hears anything,
post it in the group.

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:08.360 line:100%
Right.

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:10.240 line:100%
Great idea!

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:12.640 line:100%
-Right.
-Good idea.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:15.360 line:100%
Scan the code.

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:16.400 line:100%
HE YUANHANG

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:17.800 line:100%
DAD, DON'T LET THEM FOOL YOU
ONCE YOU'RE IN, IT'S HARD TO BACK OUT

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:28.080 line:100%
-Are you in?
-Yes.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:29.960 line:100%
-All in?
-Yes.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.120 line:100%
I only notified a few of you.
Who else is coming?

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:35.600 line:100%
-Isn't this everyone?
-Yeah.

00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:36.600 line:100%
No one else.

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:45.520 line:100%
Officer He,

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:49.240 line:100%
this building is run-down and creepy.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:52.640 line:100%
Moving in here is bad for your health.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.520 line:100%
What if your situation relapses?

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:57.240 line:100%
You're not my son.

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:59.120 line:100%
-You don't need to worry about my health.
-He Yuanhang,

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.360 line:100%
you're not a police officer now,
and you're not an owner here either.

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:05.400 line:100%
Stop causing trouble
for the Redevelopment Bureau.

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:06.320 line:100%
Jeez.

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:10.120 line:100%
Open your eyes wide and look carefully.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:10.960 line:100%
LEASE AGREEMENT

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:14.440 line:100%
There's a signature and a stamp.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.600 line:100%
I'm a legal tenant.

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:18.640 line:100%
Who's causing trouble now?

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:22.760 line:100%
Money-grubber, you played tricks
on our demolition agreement.

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:25.080 line:100%
You promised compensation
and didn't deliver.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:28.600 line:100%
If you want to tear down my home,
that'll be at least ten million.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.640 line:100%
Not one single dime less.

00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:32.120 line:100%
Ten million!

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:33.640 line:100%
Ten million!

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:35.280 line:100%
Ten million!

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:37.160 line:100%
Ten million!

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:38.480 line:100%
Ten million!

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:40.840 line:100%
-We did it!
-We won!

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:42.800 line:100%
Drink some tea.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:44.160 line:100%
Drink tea.

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:45.480 line:100%
Carry on.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.080 line:100%
Is the water ready?

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:51.240 line:20%
YUANLONGLI INTERNATIONAL GARDEN

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.480 line:100%
-Start the chant.
-Let's go.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.560 line:100%
As long as we still have our homes,

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:59.360 line:100%
we can wait!

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:01.200 line:100%
Bad terms?

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:03.320 line:100%
We're not selling!

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.280 line:100%
As long as we still have our homes,

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.880 line:100%
we can wait!

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:12.880 line:100%
Dad, can't you clean up tomorrow?

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.960 line:100%
The real work hasn't even started.

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:17.800 line:100%
Go home and sleep
after everything is done.

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:21.440 line:100%
Are you sure you don't need me here?

00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:23.000 line:100%
We're partners this time.

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:24.800 line:100%
I manage inside. You take the outside.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.640 line:100%
We'll block them from both sides.

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.600 line:100%
There's no way we can't crack this case.

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:30.920 line:100%
Get up. Get to work.

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:38.040 line:100%
Open the windows wider.

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:51.320 line:20%
FAKE BLUE LEATHER HEELS

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:04.720 line:100%
Dad, even the task force
can't match this setup.

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:08.800 line:100%
Before troops move, supplies go first.

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:13.160 line:100%
Team Leader He, what are your next orders?

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:15.400 line:100%
I'm not a team leader.

00:22:15.920 --> 00:22:17.960 line:100%
The team leader is Ran.

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:19.360 line:100%
What we need to do now

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:21.880 line:100%
is guess what his next move would be.

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:25.720 line:100%
If I were him,

00:22:26.800 --> 00:22:30.440 line:100%
once I got to Yuanlongli,
I'd first use Tremaux's algorithm.

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:34.840 line:100%
I'll do the building canvass.

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:38.200 line:100%
Tomorrow, I'll go through every place
in this building

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:39.680 line:100%
connected to the June 30th case.

00:22:40.600 --> 00:22:41.640 line:100%
I'll go to the property management

00:22:41.720 --> 00:22:44.560 line:100%
and check the resident
and tenant list from 2002.

00:22:44.640 --> 00:22:46.840 line:100%
And ask whether Uncle Ran
visited any of them back then.

00:22:47.440 --> 00:22:49.720 line:100%
Good. That's the plan.

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:52.000 line:100%
Go home now. Rest up early.

00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:02.480 line:100%
How come you're older now,

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:03.840 line:100%
but still full of energy?

00:23:04.440 --> 00:23:07.840 line:100%
I have more than enough strength
to handle ten men alone.

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:10.880 line:100%
Remember to take
your blood pressure medicine.

00:23:10.960 --> 00:23:12.920 line:100%
The wind gets strong at night.
Remember to close the windows.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:15.880 line:100%
You're so naggy. Go on.

00:24:44.120 --> 00:24:46.800 line:100%
I'm leaving, sir.

00:24:49.080 --> 00:24:49.920 line:100%
Ran,

00:24:52.360 --> 00:24:54.320 line:100%
you always saw me as your mentor.

00:24:57.200 --> 00:24:59.240 line:100%
But you're the one who taught me.

00:25:28.080 --> 00:25:29.440 line:20%
2002 YUANLONGLI RESIDENTIAL
COMPLEX OWNER/TENANT REGISTRATION FORM

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:50.120 line:100%
My goodness! Run!

00:26:50.200 --> 00:26:51.240 line:100%
Hey!

00:27:38.240 --> 00:27:41.320 line:100%
Du Mingliang, can I count you as a human?

00:27:41.400 --> 00:27:44.000 line:100%
Playing games all day long.

00:27:44.080 --> 00:27:46.240 line:100%
I'd rather have given birth
to a bun than you.

00:28:35.840 --> 00:28:37.200 line:100%
Mr. He. Bollard!

00:28:41.560 --> 00:28:44.920 line:100%
Mr. He, I heard you moved in.

00:28:46.560 --> 00:28:49.160 line:100%
Many people moved out.
When are you planning to move?

00:28:49.240 --> 00:28:50.400 line:100%
I'm not moving.

00:28:50.480 --> 00:28:52.400 line:100%
I signed a long-term lease.

00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:54.240 line:100%
I spent a lot of money
renovating the shop.

00:28:54.840 --> 00:28:56.320 line:100%
That money-grubber

00:28:56.400 --> 00:28:58.440 line:100%
tries to tear down illegally
and not pay me a dime.

00:28:58.520 --> 00:29:01.120 line:100%
That's ridiculous.
I'm fighting him to the end.

00:29:02.560 --> 00:29:03.560 line:100%
Join this group chat.

00:29:05.160 --> 00:29:07.320 line:100%
Holdouts Group? What's this for?

00:29:07.400 --> 00:29:08.280 line:100%
We're all on the same side.

00:29:08.360 --> 00:29:10.040 line:100%
Oh, so you made a group there.

00:29:11.520 --> 00:29:13.800 line:100%
Mr. He, why did you move in
at a time like this?

00:29:13.880 --> 00:29:14.960 line:100%
Working on a case?

00:29:15.600 --> 00:29:16.840 line:100%
Let me ask you this.

00:29:16.920 --> 00:29:19.080 line:100%
In the winter of 2002,

00:29:19.160 --> 00:29:20.720 line:100%
did you see Officer Ran?

00:29:25.240 --> 00:29:27.360 line:100%
I wasn't supposed to tell you.

00:29:28.080 --> 00:29:30.520 line:100%
But now I guess I can.

00:29:31.680 --> 00:29:32.520 line:100%
Go on.

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:35.560 line:100%
Come out here!

00:29:35.640 --> 00:29:37.880 line:100%
If you don't give me back the mouse,

00:29:37.960 --> 00:29:39.360 line:100%
I'll go on a hunger strike for a month!

00:29:39.440 --> 00:29:40.840 line:100%
Oh, I'm so scared of you.

00:29:40.920 --> 00:29:42.560 line:100%
A whole month of hunger strike?

00:29:44.160 --> 00:29:46.080 line:100%
-Madam.
-Officer Ran,

00:29:46.160 --> 00:29:47.760 line:100%
perfect timing.

00:29:47.840 --> 00:29:50.600 line:100%
Help me drag this brat out.

00:29:50.680 --> 00:29:53.520 line:100%
You won't let me be a cybercafe manager
or open a cybercafé.

00:29:53.600 --> 00:29:55.640 line:100%
Then I'll open the window
and live on air then.

00:29:55.720 --> 00:29:56.960 line:100%
Go ahead.

00:29:57.040 --> 00:29:58.560 line:100%
No one's scared of you.

00:30:03.040 --> 00:30:05.000 line:100%
Du Mingliang, listen to me.

00:30:05.080 --> 00:30:07.560 line:100%
Whether to be a manager
or open a cybercafé,

00:30:07.640 --> 00:30:09.160 line:100%
you first need technical skills.

00:30:09.240 --> 00:30:11.120 line:100%
There are courses online now.

00:30:11.200 --> 00:30:14.000 line:100%
You can sign up for computer science
and study at home.

00:30:15.040 --> 00:30:16.000 line:100%
Where did you see that?

00:30:16.600 --> 00:30:18.960 line:100%
I can register it for you.
But first, you need to eat.

00:30:20.760 --> 00:30:22.880 line:100%
Come out first.

00:30:22.960 --> 00:30:24.400 line:100%
Eat your dinner.

00:30:29.920 --> 00:30:31.320 line:100%
Jeez.

00:30:32.440 --> 00:30:35.240 line:100%
Madam, let me ask you something.

00:30:35.320 --> 00:30:38.960 line:100%
Did you see any strangers
go into No. 1703 this summer?

00:30:39.040 --> 00:30:41.040 line:100%
You mean the Wu family?

00:30:41.760 --> 00:30:44.680 line:100%
Their door is always shut.

00:30:44.760 --> 00:30:46.600 line:100%
I only saw it open once.

00:30:46.680 --> 00:30:49.080 line:100%
At the time,
the whole place was full of police.

00:30:58.360 --> 00:31:02.360 line:100%
Right, have you seen
double-layer leather shoes?

00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:04.040 line:100%
What is that?

00:31:04.680 --> 00:31:07.360 line:100%
Shoes with one layer inside
and another layer wrapped outside.

00:31:07.440 --> 00:31:08.840 line:100%
Counterfeit designer shoes.

00:31:10.920 --> 00:31:12.520 line:100%
I have seen

00:31:12.600 --> 00:31:14.240 line:100%
cardboard shoes before.

00:31:14.320 --> 00:31:16.280 line:100%
Whoever made those
double-layer leather shoes

00:31:17.200 --> 00:31:19.680 line:100%
must've had something wrong up top.

00:31:19.760 --> 00:31:21.240 line:100%
Why wrap another layer

00:31:21.320 --> 00:31:23.320 line:100%
over a perfectly good pair of shoes?

00:31:24.160 --> 00:31:25.760 line:100%
I have seen that kind of shoes.

00:31:25.840 --> 00:31:27.440 line:100%
The person making shoes like that

00:31:27.520 --> 00:31:29.680 line:100%
must be a very experienced craftsman.

00:31:30.480 --> 00:31:32.520 line:100%
Think about it. Two layers of leather

00:31:32.600 --> 00:31:35.560 line:100%
and still made to look
exactly like the real thing.

00:31:35.640 --> 00:31:38.160 line:100%
You know, that's not easy.

00:31:38.240 --> 00:31:39.680 line:100%
Do you know any craftsmen like this?

00:31:40.880 --> 00:31:41.920 line:100%
No.

00:31:42.880 --> 00:31:46.120 line:100%
But you can ask those who sell fake shoes.

00:31:46.200 --> 00:31:48.240 line:100%
They would definitely know.

00:31:51.560 --> 00:31:53.400 line:100%
<i>Then Officer Ran left.</i>

00:31:54.360 --> 00:31:56.640 line:100%
Before leaving,
he specifically told me this.

00:31:56.720 --> 00:31:58.080 line:100%
If I ran into you,

00:31:58.160 --> 00:32:00.720 line:100%
I must not tell you that he had come by

00:32:00.800 --> 00:32:03.120 line:100%
or what questions he asked.

00:32:03.840 --> 00:32:06.240 line:100%
Mr. He, aren't you his mentor?

00:32:06.320 --> 00:32:07.520 line:100%
Why would he hide it from you?

00:32:08.920 --> 00:32:10.120 line:100%
Double-layer leather shoes.

00:32:11.880 --> 00:32:13.320 line:100%
Fake shoe sellers.

00:32:15.880 --> 00:32:18.640 line:100%
Right. Guess what I saw
at the night market.

00:32:19.160 --> 00:32:21.560 line:100%
Those same blue leather heels
the missing woman wore

00:32:21.640 --> 00:32:22.880 line:100%
are called Double Fish.

00:32:22.960 --> 00:32:24.920 line:100%
Seems like a name brand. Pretty expensive.

00:32:26.560 --> 00:32:29.720 line:100%
So why didn't you clear your head too?

00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:33.080 line:100%
You think branded shoes sold
at the night market are real?

00:32:37.680 --> 00:32:40.240 line:100%
Mr. He. You're leaving?

00:32:40.320 --> 00:32:42.400 line:100%
Put the property list aside for now.

00:32:42.480 --> 00:32:43.840 line:100%
Go to the Commerce Bureau.

00:32:43.920 --> 00:32:45.680 line:100%
Check the list of shoe and hat vendors

00:32:45.760 --> 00:32:48.480 line:100%
at the Riverside Night Market in 1997.

00:32:49.040 --> 00:32:50.480 line:100%
Contact them one by one.

00:32:50.560 --> 00:32:53.040 line:100%
Ask whether Ran went
looking for them back then.

00:32:53.120 --> 00:32:54.560 line:100%
<i>All vendors?</i>

00:32:54.640 --> 00:32:55.800 line:100%
Every single one.

00:32:55.880 --> 00:32:57.560 line:100%
<i>That's a huge workload.</i>

00:32:57.640 --> 00:32:58.640 line:100%
Hurry up.

00:32:59.440 --> 00:33:01.120 line:100%
Give us a straight answer.

00:33:01.200 --> 00:33:03.720 line:100%
Can the relocation payout
still be negotiated or not?

00:33:03.800 --> 00:33:06.800 line:100%
Otherwise, we old folks here
would rather die

00:33:06.880 --> 00:33:09.200 line:100%
right here in Yuanlongli.

00:33:09.280 --> 00:33:11.440 line:100%
Right! We'll die right here in Yuanlongli!

00:33:11.520 --> 00:33:12.880 line:100%
As long as we still have our homes,

00:33:12.960 --> 00:33:14.920 line:100%
we can wait!

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:16.640 line:100%
Bad terms?

00:33:16.720 --> 00:33:18.080 line:100%
We're not selling!

00:33:18.160 --> 00:33:20.080 line:100%
Everyone, please calm down.

00:33:20.160 --> 00:33:22.040 line:100%
Kick up all the fuss you want.

00:33:22.120 --> 00:33:24.360 line:100%
Not one extra dime
will be added to the compensation.

00:33:24.440 --> 00:33:26.000 line:100%
-You!
-When the time comes,

00:33:26.080 --> 00:33:28.120 line:100%
I'll bring the demolition crew
and bury explosives here.

00:33:28.200 --> 00:33:29.120 line:100%
Whoever won't leave,

00:33:29.200 --> 00:33:31.120 line:100%
I'll bury explosives at their front door.

00:33:31.200 --> 00:33:33.600 line:100%
-How can you say this?
-Qian, you bastard!

00:33:33.680 --> 00:33:34.680 line:100%
If you dare do that,

00:33:34.760 --> 00:33:36.360 line:100%
I'll drag you down with me!

00:33:36.440 --> 00:33:38.440 line:100%
Exactly! Go down together!

00:33:39.160 --> 00:33:40.760 line:100%
-Alright, everyone.
-Go down together!

00:33:40.840 --> 00:33:42.640 line:100%
Will you stop already?

00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:45.480 line:100%
I'm the project manager here.
You just need to cooperate.

00:33:45.560 --> 00:33:46.400 line:100%
We're all old neighbors.

00:33:46.480 --> 00:33:48.120 line:100%
Is there any point in bluffing
and tricking them like this?

00:33:48.960 --> 00:33:49.800 line:100%
I cooperate with you?

00:33:50.720 --> 00:33:53.680 line:100%
Everyone from Yuanlongli knows
what kind of person you used to be.

00:33:59.160 --> 00:34:02.200 line:100%
Some people have dirty minds.

00:34:02.280 --> 00:34:03.440 line:100%
So everything they see looks dirty.

00:34:05.800 --> 00:34:06.640 line:100%
Officer He,

00:34:07.360 --> 00:34:09.519 line:100%
this is a matter for the owners.

00:34:09.600 --> 00:34:11.479 line:100%
You're just a tenant.
You don't get a share of the money, right?

00:34:13.840 --> 00:34:16.680 line:100%
Qian, you're not young anymore.

00:34:17.479 --> 00:34:19.360 line:100%
You should really do something
about your bad breath.

00:34:20.720 --> 00:34:22.080 line:100%
Well said!

00:34:22.160 --> 00:34:24.039 line:100%
Exactly right!

00:34:26.560 --> 00:34:27.680 line:100%
Let me make this clear.

00:34:27.760 --> 00:34:31.360 line:100%
Everyone should raise demands
reasonably and legally.

00:34:31.439 --> 00:34:32.999 line:100%
Don't act without order.

00:34:33.680 --> 00:34:35.959 line:100%
Qiao is only doing her job.

00:34:36.039 --> 00:34:37.560 line:100%
But the way she handles things

00:34:37.640 --> 00:34:39.479 line:100%
is nothing like certain people.

00:34:40.080 --> 00:34:42.519 line:100%
So don't lash out at everybody.

00:34:42.600 --> 00:34:43.840 line:100%
Can you do that?

00:34:49.200 --> 00:34:52.200 line:100%
Can't do it? Then I'm leaving
the group chat right now.

00:34:52.800 --> 00:34:54.400 line:100%
-Please!
-No!

00:34:54.479 --> 00:34:56.320 line:100%
-Officer He!
-Officer He,

00:34:57.080 --> 00:34:59.480 line:100%
what you just said
was deeply philosophical.

00:35:00.200 --> 00:35:03.200 line:100%
From now on, we won't
make things hard for Miss Qiao.

00:35:03.280 --> 00:35:04.120 line:100%
-We won't do that.
-That's right.

00:35:04.200 --> 00:35:05.000 line:100%
We won't do that to her.

00:35:05.080 --> 00:35:06.200 line:100%
No.

00:35:07.200 --> 00:35:09.680 line:100%
We'll go after the one
who's really to blame.

00:35:09.760 --> 00:35:11.080 line:100%
-That's right.
-We'll go after the one

00:35:11.160 --> 00:35:12.120 line:100%
who's really to blame.

00:35:12.200 --> 00:35:14.240 line:100%
As long as we still have our homes,

00:35:14.320 --> 00:35:16.080 line:100%
we can wait!

00:35:16.160 --> 00:35:18.000 line:100%
Bad terms?

00:35:18.080 --> 00:35:20.280 line:100%
As long as we still have our homes…

00:35:20.360 --> 00:35:22.480 line:100%
As long as we still have our homes,

00:35:22.560 --> 00:35:24.520 line:100%
we can wait!

00:35:24.600 --> 00:35:26.400 line:100%
Bad terms?

00:35:26.480 --> 00:35:28.480 line:100%
We're not selling!

00:35:28.560 --> 00:35:30.680 line:100%
Qiao, don't worry.

00:35:30.760 --> 00:35:33.120 line:100%
As long as I'm here,
nothing will go wrong.

00:35:33.880 --> 00:35:35.440 line:100%
Thank you, Mr. He.

00:35:36.360 --> 00:35:39.720 line:100%
There's something I'd like
to ask for your help with.

00:35:41.640 --> 00:35:42.480 line:100%
Can you think of a way

00:35:42.560 --> 00:35:45.480 line:100%
to delay the demolition deadline
a little longer?

00:35:46.160 --> 00:35:47.200 line:100%
Mr. He,

00:35:48.040 --> 00:35:50.800 line:100%
why did you get involved in this too?

00:35:50.880 --> 00:35:52.880 line:100%
Ran left with regret.

00:35:54.360 --> 00:35:57.200 line:100%
I have to stay in Yuanlongli for a while

00:35:57.280 --> 00:35:59.920 line:100%
and help him make up for it
and fulfill his wish.

00:36:08.160 --> 00:36:09.000 line:100%
Alright.

00:36:09.920 --> 00:36:11.160 line:100%
I'll do my best to help.

00:36:26.280 --> 00:36:28.240 line:100%
Mister, please do me a favor.

00:36:28.320 --> 00:36:29.840 line:100%
I'll remember you for life.

00:36:41.360 --> 00:36:43.400 line:100%
TO LET

00:36:53.040 --> 00:36:54.000 line:100%
CALL

00:36:57.320 --> 00:36:58.320 line:100%
<i>Hello?</i>

00:36:58.400 --> 00:36:59.680 line:100%
Hello?

00:36:59.760 --> 00:37:02.080 line:100%
I'd like to ask about the shop
you had for rent.

00:37:02.160 --> 00:37:04.840 line:100%
Did you rent it to a woman
who sold shoes in 1997?

00:37:05.480 --> 00:37:07.640 line:100%
<i>1997? I can't remember.</i>

00:37:07.720 --> 00:37:09.680 line:100%
She had short hair and was very outgoing.

00:37:09.760 --> 00:37:11.440 line:100%
Whenever someone passed her shop,

00:37:11.520 --> 00:37:13.320 line:100%
she'd pull them over to look at her shoes.

00:37:13.920 --> 00:37:15.360 line:100%
And she would say things like,

00:37:16.160 --> 00:37:18.000 line:100%
"Please do me a favor, mister.

00:37:18.080 --> 00:37:20.560 line:100%
I'll remember you for life."

00:37:21.200 --> 00:37:23.680 line:100%
<i>Now I remember. That must be Liu Guifang.</i>

00:37:23.760 --> 00:37:25.400 line:100%
<i>She couldn't afford the rent anymore.</i>

00:37:25.480 --> 00:37:26.920 line:100%
<i>She insisted on using</i>
<i>her stock to cover it.</i>

00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:28.320 line:100%
<i>Those were the exact words she used.</i>

00:37:28.920 --> 00:37:30.960 line:100%
<i>I felt soft-hearted at the time,</i>
<i>so I let it slide.</i>

00:37:31.040 --> 00:37:32.240 line:100%
Where did she go after that?

00:37:52.360 --> 00:37:54.800 line:100%
I called you.
Why was your phone off again?

00:37:54.880 --> 00:37:57.280 line:100%
Do you know how many vendors

00:37:57.360 --> 00:37:58.680 line:100%
there were at
Riverside Night Market in 1997?

00:37:59.280 --> 00:38:00.200 line:100%
More than 500.

00:38:00.280 --> 00:38:02.000 line:100%
Even if I had three phones,
they would all be dead by now.

00:38:03.560 --> 00:38:04.560 line:100%
Did you find anything?

00:38:06.400 --> 00:38:10.920 line:100%
Uncle Ran contacted
someone named Liu Guifang.

00:38:11.920 --> 00:38:12.880 line:100%
Here.

00:38:12.960 --> 00:38:13.800 line:100%
LIU GUIFANG

00:38:43.720 --> 00:38:45.640 line:100%
MAHJONG AND TEA,WELCOME INSIDE

00:38:48.040 --> 00:38:50.760 line:100%
<i>I heard Liu Guifang got together</i>
<i>with the owner of a mahjong parlor.</i>

00:38:50.840 --> 00:38:52.200 line:100%
<i>He received a hefty demolition payout</i>

00:38:52.280 --> 00:38:53.800 line:100%
<i>from several houses</i>
<i>he owned in the village.</i>

00:38:53.880 --> 00:38:54.920 line:100%
<i>He got rich long ago.</i>

00:39:12.040 --> 00:39:14.440 line:100%
Come on. Be generous.

00:39:14.520 --> 00:39:16.400 line:100%
Just do me a favor, mister.

00:39:16.480 --> 00:39:17.960 line:100%
I'll remember you for life.

00:39:22.280 --> 00:39:24.680 line:100%
Alright. I'm hanging up now, Yao.

00:39:26.120 --> 00:39:28.320 line:100%
-Excuse me.
-Playing mahjong?

00:39:28.400 --> 00:39:30.000 line:100%
Five years ago,
at the Riverside Night Market,

00:39:30.080 --> 00:39:31.800 line:100%
you sold me a pair of fake leather shoes.

00:39:31.880 --> 00:39:32.880 line:100%
They were cardboard shoes.

00:39:32.960 --> 00:39:34.640 line:100%
What? Five years ago?

00:39:38.880 --> 00:39:39.880 line:100%
It's been five years.

00:39:40.480 --> 00:39:43.600 line:100%
Mister, you really hold grudges.

00:39:45.440 --> 00:39:47.240 line:100%
I definitely don't remember you.

00:39:47.320 --> 00:39:49.240 line:100%
But back then, I did sell fake shoes.

00:39:50.320 --> 00:39:53.000 line:100%
How about this?
I'll pay you ten times the price.

00:39:53.080 --> 00:39:54.320 line:100%
Is that okay?

00:40:02.560 --> 00:40:04.680 line:100%
You sold Double Fish back then.

00:40:04.760 --> 00:40:05.760 line:100%
They came in several colors.

00:40:05.840 --> 00:40:06.880 line:100%
Do you know who in Weiyang

00:40:06.960 --> 00:40:08.800 line:100%
could make this kind
of double-layer leather heels?

00:40:08.880 --> 00:40:10.360 line:100%
Double-layer leather heels?

00:40:10.960 --> 00:40:12.280 line:100%
Let me see.

00:40:14.320 --> 00:40:15.320 line:100%
Don't open it.

00:40:18.160 --> 00:40:20.320 line:100%
Double-layer leather heels…
That's pretty unusual.

00:40:20.920 --> 00:40:23.240 line:100%
Judging from the finish and workmanship,

00:40:23.320 --> 00:40:25.920 line:100%
that should be Mr. Lu
from Pingzhao County.

00:40:26.760 --> 00:40:27.800 line:100%
Bet you didn't know.

00:40:27.880 --> 00:40:30.520 line:100%
Mr. Lu was a master
of fake shoes in Weiyang.

00:40:30.600 --> 00:40:32.680 line:100%
The shoes he made
could pass for the real thing.

00:40:33.920 --> 00:40:35.320 line:100%
Pingzhao County.

00:40:38.480 --> 00:40:39.640 line:100%
MAP

00:40:41.680 --> 00:40:44.840 line:20%
PINGZHAO COUNTY

00:40:56.920 --> 00:41:00.200 line:100%
PINGZHAO COUNTY

00:41:00.960 --> 00:41:02.200 line:100%
It's been 13 years.

00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:05.640 line:100%
No idea whether Mr. Lu is still around.

00:41:07.800 --> 00:41:09.360 line:100%
NO. 6, LU VILLAGE, BEISHI TOWN
PINGZHAO COUNTY, WEIYANG CITY

00:41:09.440 --> 00:41:12.160 line:100%
Uncle Ran probably
has taken this road too.

00:41:15.360 --> 00:41:17.160 line:100%
We've picked the trail back up at last.